{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>וַיְכַס הֶעָנָן אֶת אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד וּכְבוֹד ה׳ מָלֵא אֶת הַמִּשְׁכָּן.</b> It appears from this that כְּבוֹד ה׳ is not the cloud, but rather the fire and the light — which is כְּבוֹד ה׳ — was seen from within the cloud, for without the cloud it would not have been possible to gaze upon it, for in the light of the sun a person cannot gaze — how much more so in the light of the splendor of His Shekhinah, blessed be He. Therefore that holy light was always seen from within the cloud. But when the מִּשְׁכָּן was erected, they were separated from one another, for the divine light entered into the מִּשְׁכָּן, for there is the place of His holiness, blessed be He, and the cloud remained outside. And this is what it says at the end of parashat Mishpatim (Exodus 24:16): ״וַיִּשְׁכֹּן כְּבוֹד ה׳ עַל הַר סִינַי וַיְכַסֵּהוּ הֶעָנָן שֵׁשֶׁת יָמִים״ — that is to say, the cloud covered כְּבוֹד ה׳ so that they would be able to see that glory, as it says there: ״וּמַרְאֵה כְּבוֹד ה׳ כְּאֵשׁ אֹכֶלֶת בְּרֹאשׁ הָהָר לְעֵינֵי כָּל יִשְׂרָאֵל״, for in this manner they were able to see the glory. And therefore it says here: ״וְלֹא יָכֹל מֹשֶׁה לָבוֹא אֶל אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד כִּי שָׁכַן עָלָיו הֶעָנָן וּכְבוֹד ה׳ מָלֵא הַמִּשְׁכָּן״ — for had כְּבוֹד ה׳ been intermingled with the cloud, he would have been able to enter there, as it is stated at the end of parashat Mishpatim: ״וַיָּבֹא מֹשֶׁה בְּתוֹךְ הֶעָנָן״ — for since at that time כְּבוֹד ה׳ was covered by the cloud, it was possible for Moses to enter within the cloud. But now that they were separated from one another — the cloud being outside and כְּבוֹד ה׳ being inside the אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד without any cloud — therefore it was impossible for Moses to enter within the אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד; yet up to the אֹהֶל מוֹעֵד, right next to it, he could come, even though the cloud rested upon it. And according to these words of ours, many difficulties concerning this matter that the commentators have raised will be resolved." "<b>The book of Exodus is concluded — with the help of the Giver of might and strength.</b>"], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:25:53.478566806Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}